    "body": "Fixes #1572\n\nSetting cython_compile_time_env on an Extension only worked if the build went through the distutils build_ext, because that is the path that reads the attribute and passes it to cythonize() as an option. Calling cythonize() directly with the same Extension silently ignored it, and the compile then failed with \"Compile-time name ... not defined\" if the module actually used the name. I reproduced exactly that on master before changing anything.\n\nThe change is in Cython/Build/Dependencies.py:\n\n- create_extension_list() now keeps the attribute when it rebuilds an Extension from the template, since it is not part of the distutils settings it copies over.\n- In cythonize(), when a module has its own env, it is merged over the global compile_time_env for that module only, so two extensions with different envs can be built in one call.\n\nTests: new Cython/Build/Tests/TestCythonizeCompileTimeEnv.py covers the per extension env on its own, plus a two module call where one module overrides the global env and the other falls back to it. The surrounding Build test modules (TestDependencies, TestRecythonize, TestCythonizeArgsParser, TestCyCache, 91 tests) still pass, and the original repro from the issue now compiles with the env applied.",
    "closed_at": null,
